        2080,
        1889
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "In accordance with the following standard procedures and specifications for which the People of the City of New York are eligible, the City's Delegative Representative will be elected and will be responsible to the People of the City of New York, as follows:\n\n1. The People of the City of New York will be elected for a term of two years, beginning on the first of the following September, and will be reelected for a term of two years, beginning on the first of the following September, and so on ad infinitum.\n\n2. The People of the City of New York will be elected for a term of two years, beginning on the first of the following September, and will be reelected for a term of two years, beginning on the first of the following September, and so on ad infinitum.\n\n3. These persons will be elected and reelected on the basis of the first of the following September, and will be reelected for a term of two years, beginning on the first of the following September, and so on ad infinitum.",
